      "text": "**I’d skip the outdoor walk right now.** In Singapore it’s already 12:46 p.m. on Saturday, October 17, and it’s raining at about 31°C; the forecast is hot, with more showers and a high around 33°C. \n\nA gentle indoor walk is a safer choice for now. If she goes out later, wait until the rain and any lightning have passed, keep it short and easy, and check the local heat-stress advisory first. Singapore’s Health Ministry advises older adults to take extra care when heat stress is elevated. ([moh.gov.sg](https://www.moh.gov.sg/newsroom/using-findings-of-heat-map-study-to-help-elderly-recognise-common-symptoms-of-heat-related-illnesses-and-seek-timely-medical-advice/?utm_source=openai))",
